1
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:06,930
There we go!

2
00:00:07,890 --> 00:00:09,270
Over here!

3
00:00:18,530 --> 00:00:20,570
- Are you ready?
- Ready!

4
00:00:23,030 --> 00:00:24,620
Hey, come on!

5
00:00:25,370 --> 00:00:27,330
Stop sending the ball this way.

6
00:00:27,410 --> 00:00:28,540
There we go!

7
00:00:29,370 --> 00:00:31,830
Look over there.

8
00:00:31,910 --> 00:00:33,950
In the middle of the day.

9
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:41,720
She hangs around here, too?

10
00:00:47,140 --> 00:00:48,810
Hey, Chimney!

11
00:00:48,890 --> 00:00:50,560
Can you get the ball for us?

12
00:00:58,190 --> 00:01:00,780
Let me play with you guys.

13
00:01:00,860 --> 00:01:02,110
What?

14
00:01:02,190 --> 00:01:03,980
Heads up, Chimney!

15
00:01:17,670 --> 00:01:19,010
Get the ball from her!

16
00:01:19,090 --> 00:01:20,130
Go!

17
00:01:31,100 --> 00:01:33,810
- I can't focus.
- I can't focus.

18
00:01:39,230 --> 00:01:40,610
You okay, Chimney?

19
00:01:40,690 --> 00:01:42,190
Puke cat.

20
00:01:42,280 --> 00:01:43,490
I can't move.

21
00:01:43,570 --> 00:01:45,070
It's only been two minutes.

22
00:01:45,650 --> 00:01:47,650
So this is aging.

23
00:01:47,740 --> 00:01:49,030
It's definitely the cigarettes.

24
00:01:49,120 --> 00:01:50,620
Should we call an ambulance?

25
00:01:50,700 --> 00:01:54,200
Hold on, I'll be able to recover
once I smoke.

26
00:01:54,290 --> 00:01:55,460
Excuse me.

27
00:01:56,790 --> 00:02:00,540
We received a report
of a suspicious person chasing children.

28
00:02:03,130 --> 00:02:05,170
You need to be more careful.

29
00:02:05,260 --> 00:02:08,050
You think it's okay, 
just because this is Nyagamihara?

30
00:02:15,770 --> 00:02:17,900
- You can't smoke in the park!
- How awful.

31
00:02:17,980 --> 00:02:19,940
- And right after I just warned you.
- Honestly.

32
00:04:38,370 --> 00:04:40,000
It stinks!

33
00:04:43,540 --> 00:04:44,420
What the actual hell?

34
00:04:46,080 --> 00:04:46,910
It smells so bad.

35
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:50,840
It's like a mix of coffee, cigarettes, 
and old feet!

36
00:04:50,920 --> 00:04:54,470
It smells like human malice
and bitterness!

37
00:04:54,550 --> 00:04:56,550
Yes, this is

38
00:04:56,640 --> 00:04:59,310
Jakusobubura!

39
00:04:59,390 --> 00:05:01,560
JAKUSOBUBURA

40
00:05:01,640 --> 00:05:03,770
Yani Neko! We gotta evacuate!

41
00:05:03,850 --> 00:05:07,310
More stink will rain down on us
if we don't get out of here!

42
00:05:08,690 --> 00:05:11,360
This is bad. Like, seriously bad for you.

43
00:05:11,440 --> 00:05:15,610
There are over 70 carcinogens
in cigarettes.

44
00:05:16,910 --> 00:05:22,370
Not to mention the secondhand smoke
affecting non-smokers like me.

45
00:05:22,450 --> 00:05:24,870
You get what I'm saying, Yani Neko?

46
00:05:24,960 --> 00:05:27,250
You double your risk of having a stroke, 

47
00:05:27,330 --> 00:05:28,830
and it deteriorates your vessels.

48
00:05:28,920 --> 00:05:30,380
Recent research shows

49
00:05:30,460 --> 00:05:33,880
something about it
causing heart failure or something.

50
00:05:33,970 --> 00:05:35,350
YANI NEKO'S TEMPER

51
00:05:35,430 --> 00:05:36,390
Hey!

52
00:05:36,470 --> 00:05:38,470
So, I wanted to tell you

53
00:05:38,550 --> 00:05:41,600
a friend of mine started
a local smoking cessation workshop.

54
00:05:41,680 --> 00:05:43,930
I brought you a pamphlet today.

55
00:05:44,020 --> 00:05:45,270
Let's see here.

56
00:05:45,350 --> 00:05:47,520
Damn it, I can't see.

57
00:05:48,610 --> 00:05:50,320
Where is it? What is this? Gross!

58
00:05:51,520 --> 00:05:52,650
Is this it?

59
00:05:52,730 --> 00:05:53,940
NYACOTINE PATCH

60
00:05:54,030 --> 00:05:55,410
No, that's not it.

61
00:05:59,280 --> 00:06:01,240
You've got a face
on the back of your head too!

62
00:06:01,330 --> 00:06:04,290
Now you're part
of the nicotine addicts club, too!

63
00:06:07,670 --> 00:06:12,930
DO NOT USE ON HUMANS.
IT MAY CAUSE DEATH.

64
00:06:19,180 --> 00:06:23,560
Sorry, can you wait until my face heals?
What is it?

65
00:06:25,390 --> 00:06:28,190
What the hell did you stick on my head, 
you dumb cat?

66
00:06:30,810 --> 00:06:32,940
Wait, I'm feeling…

67
00:06:38,400 --> 00:06:41,200
Is this guilt?

68
00:06:41,780 --> 00:06:45,280
I mean, this terribly-mannered cat
is completely at fault.

69
00:06:45,370 --> 00:06:47,910
But maybe I'm being too condescending.

70
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:48,960
USE APPROPRIATELY

71
00:06:49,040 --> 00:06:54,960
I'm always using my righteousness
to make myself feel better.

72
00:06:55,050 --> 00:06:59,180
Yani Neko, sorry, I went too far.

73
00:07:00,180 --> 00:07:01,060
What?

74
00:07:24,200 --> 00:07:26,080
What are you doing?

75
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:35,130
That's the stuff.

76
00:07:37,210 --> 00:07:39,000
Chainsmoker Cat!

77
00:08:16,380 --> 00:08:17,470
Okay.

78
00:08:29,350 --> 00:08:32,020
At least be done after just one!

79
00:08:33,190 --> 00:08:34,820
Do you understand your situation?

80
00:08:34,900 --> 00:08:35,780
Yes, sir.

81
00:08:35,860 --> 00:08:39,240
You asked me for more time
to pay rent, that you'd do anything, 

82
00:08:39,320 --> 00:08:41,740
so I'm letting you weed the yard!

83
00:08:41,820 --> 00:08:42,659
Yes, sir.

84
00:08:42,740 --> 00:08:45,910
But you already took a cigarette break
after just five minutes.

85
00:08:45,990 --> 00:08:48,410
And then you have the gall
to start smoking a second one!

86
00:08:48,490 --> 00:08:49,570
Yes, sir.

87
00:08:49,660 --> 00:08:51,540
Stop meowing when you answer!

88
00:08:51,620 --> 00:08:52,790
Yes, sir.

89
00:08:57,500 --> 00:08:59,090
I'm confiscating this, you idiot!

90
00:08:59,880 --> 00:09:00,920
That's theft!

91
00:09:01,010 --> 00:09:05,680
In that case, you're guilty of not paying
your rent and littering cigarette butts!

92
00:09:05,760 --> 00:09:07,430
You can have this back when you're done!

93
00:09:14,810 --> 00:09:17,940
I guess I'll give her tea and snacks
after she finishes up.

94
00:09:21,150 --> 00:09:23,240
What the hell are you eating?

95
00:09:23,990 --> 00:09:26,950
Horsetails, since I'm hungry.

96
00:09:27,990 --> 00:09:30,370
Do you want some, too?

97
00:09:31,580 --> 00:09:33,290
No!

98
00:09:33,370 --> 00:09:36,040
Don't eat too much, 
or you'll get a stomachache.

99
00:09:43,170 --> 00:09:45,300
You done, Yani Neko?

100
00:09:45,380 --> 00:09:46,970
I brought you snacks.

101
00:09:50,100 --> 00:09:52,350
Wait, is she smoking?

102
00:09:52,430 --> 00:09:54,520
And what's with her belly?

103
00:09:54,600 --> 00:09:57,890
What happened to my cabbage patch?

104
00:09:58,980 --> 00:10:01,770
Are those snacks? Thanks!

105
00:10:02,940 --> 00:10:06,400
But I'm actually full right now, 
so I'll just take them home.

106
00:10:11,080 --> 00:10:14,630
My eyes! My eyes!

107
00:10:15,580 --> 00:10:17,210
Chainsmoker Cat.

108
00:10:25,970 --> 00:10:28,430
Damn that Chimney!

109
00:10:32,930 --> 00:10:34,930
She's seriously good for nothing!

110
00:10:35,020 --> 00:10:38,440
Damn it, just thinking about it
is pissing me off!

111
00:10:39,520 --> 00:10:41,440
Pissing me…

112
00:10:46,690 --> 00:10:48,690
Pissing…

113
00:10:53,280 --> 00:10:58,160
Wallpaper damage can become
a financial burden when you move out.

114
00:10:58,250 --> 00:11:00,840
Renters should be especially careful

115
00:11:00,920 --> 00:11:04,550
about discoloring the wallpaper
with cigarette smoke.

116
00:11:04,630 --> 00:11:06,470
Discoloration from smoking is considered…

117
00:11:06,550 --> 00:11:09,350
The wallpaper in my room is cream-colored.

118
00:11:10,180 --> 00:11:13,810
I'm sure it was always this color
since I air it out once in a while.

119
00:11:13,890 --> 00:11:15,980
It's definitely not from tar.

120
00:11:16,930 --> 00:11:22,060
Actually, that poster's been here
since before I moved in.

121
00:11:34,910 --> 00:11:37,910
SEALED

122
00:11:48,710 --> 00:11:51,840
You think this apartment building
is haunted?

123
00:11:51,930 --> 00:11:53,180
What are you talking about?

124
00:11:53,260 --> 00:11:54,140
Don't lie to me!

125
00:11:54,220 --> 00:11:56,640
There were strange talismans on the wall!

126
00:11:56,720 --> 00:11:59,390
I also heard ominous rapping!

127
00:11:59,480 --> 00:12:01,730
You need to tell me the truth!

128
00:12:01,810 --> 00:12:02,770
Shut up!

129
00:12:03,940 --> 00:12:05,650
I don't know what you're talking about!

130
00:12:06,610 --> 00:12:09,030
Okay, that was sus.

131
00:12:13,200 --> 00:12:14,290
That was close.

132
00:12:15,280 --> 00:12:18,070
Hug me tighter, awooh!

133
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:28,250
Hey, Yaniko.

134
00:12:28,750 --> 00:12:29,960
Yeah, Kansai?

135
00:12:30,550 --> 00:12:35,100
Didn't you tell your sister
you were going to quit smoking?

136
00:12:35,180 --> 00:12:36,390
You're still smoking?

137
00:12:37,720 --> 00:12:40,470
I'm going to quit for sure this time.

138
00:12:40,560 --> 00:12:42,650
I won't smoke anymore, starting today.

139
00:12:42,730 --> 00:12:45,400
That's the spirit.

140
00:12:50,900 --> 00:12:53,570
Yani-chan made a joke, and that's rare.

141
00:12:53,650 --> 00:12:56,400
I gotta make sure to follow up
and make it funny.

142
00:12:56,490 --> 00:12:59,280
Hold up, 
you went right back to it so fast!

143
00:12:59,370 --> 00:13:01,160
You're like a dad on his anniversary!

144
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:07,420
Do you not have a dad?

145
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:09,040
I do.

146
00:13:09,630 --> 00:13:11,760
Okay, not bad, Yani-chan.

147
00:13:11,840 --> 00:13:14,470
But us cats from the west
take pride in our humor.

148
00:13:14,550 --> 00:13:16,430
I'm not giving up without getting a laugh.

149
00:13:16,510 --> 00:13:17,680
What?

150
00:13:18,760 --> 00:13:21,800
Why do you have a nose hook?

151
00:13:22,680 --> 00:13:25,810
I found it inside this magazine
I borrowed from the landlord.

152
00:13:25,900 --> 00:13:29,200
What in the world was this doing in that?

153
00:13:29,270 --> 00:13:30,810
How do you use it?

154
00:13:31,480 --> 00:13:33,150
You hook it on your nose.

155
00:13:33,240 --> 00:13:34,320
Then you blow.

156
00:13:34,400 --> 00:13:36,320
I'd love to see you use it.

157
00:13:36,410 --> 00:13:39,540
What? Why? That's way too embarrassing.

158
00:13:39,620 --> 00:13:42,540
We're not close enough for me
to show you a funny face!

159
00:13:42,620 --> 00:13:44,080
But I'm curious.

160
00:13:44,160 --> 00:13:47,500
Curious? But that's…

161
00:13:47,580 --> 00:13:49,420
What?

162
00:13:49,500 --> 00:13:53,170
What kind of crazy request are you
making to a young maiden, you Chimney?

163
00:13:53,260 --> 00:13:55,100
But if I put this on, 

164
00:13:55,170 --> 00:13:58,090
she'll surely crack up!

165
00:13:58,680 --> 00:14:00,350
Okay, fine.

166
00:14:00,430 --> 00:14:02,890
I guess I have no choice.

167
00:14:14,400 --> 00:14:16,190
Say something!

168
00:14:19,780 --> 00:14:22,030
You damn Chimney.

169
00:14:22,120 --> 00:14:25,750
If that's how you're going to be, 
I'll have to pull out all the stops.

170
00:14:27,290 --> 00:14:28,960
What's up with those cigarettes?

171
00:14:30,040 --> 00:14:32,840
I splurged and bought some pricy smokes.

172
00:14:33,420 --> 00:14:34,710
You can't have any.

173
00:14:34,800 --> 00:14:38,720
I wasn't going to take any.
That's not what I meant.

174
00:14:38,800 --> 00:14:42,720
They're like that thing that solidifies
from microorganisms in milk?

175
00:14:42,810 --> 00:14:44,230
Wait, that's cheese!

176
00:14:46,060 --> 00:14:48,440
You can tell from cigarette sales

177
00:14:48,520 --> 00:14:51,020
the ratio of beastfolk residents
by region.

178
00:14:51,110 --> 00:14:55,490
By further leveraging animal instincts, 
selecting which brands to stock--

179
00:14:55,570 --> 00:14:57,110
Wait, that's needs!

180
00:14:58,450 --> 00:15:00,410
Boss, we're out of those things.

181
00:15:00,490 --> 00:15:02,160
Is the hardware store open now?

182
00:15:02,240 --> 00:15:05,540
You know, those long, twisty things.

183
00:15:05,620 --> 00:15:07,160
Wait, those are screws.

184
00:15:08,250 --> 00:15:11,800
The suspect is currently fleeing
towards Kariba in a Frankenstein car.

185
00:15:11,880 --> 00:15:14,930
Emergency vehicle coming through.
Please clear the way.

186
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:16,670
Wait, that's a chase.

187
00:15:20,260 --> 00:15:22,300
Wait, that's Twin Peaks!

188
00:15:30,650 --> 00:15:34,110
How about an ahegao
double peace sign then?

189
00:15:38,440 --> 00:15:41,110
Would you laugh, please?!

190
00:15:46,700 --> 00:15:49,660
Sorry, I'm sorry!

191
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:53,000
Chainsmoker Cat.

192
00:16:06,350 --> 00:16:07,770
Coming in.

193
00:16:07,850 --> 00:16:09,480
Yani-chan.

194
00:16:09,560 --> 00:16:13,650
You sure come around a lot.
Do you like me or something?

195
00:16:15,020 --> 00:16:17,560
Well, I get to drink free booze here, 

196
00:16:17,650 --> 00:16:19,690
and you don't complain if I smoke.

197
00:16:24,740 --> 00:16:28,200
Yeah? I mean, it's totally fine.

198
00:16:28,290 --> 00:16:30,290
Could you make me a drink?

199
00:16:30,370 --> 00:16:33,160
No way, I'm too lazy.

200
00:16:33,750 --> 00:16:35,670
I brought some smoked cheese.

201
00:16:36,420 --> 00:16:38,670
Okay, fine.

202
00:16:39,380 --> 00:16:40,550
Thanks.

203
00:16:43,550 --> 00:16:45,840
SUPER SIMPLE
WHISKEY AND WATER RECIPE

204
00:16:46,720 --> 00:16:51,930
Fill up a medium-sized mug
with any old whiskey until it's half full.

205
00:16:52,020 --> 00:16:54,940
Then add some sugar syrup
as much as you like.

206
00:16:55,020 --> 00:16:57,940
A couple of squirts of lemon juice.

207
00:16:58,020 --> 00:17:01,190
Then a bunch of tap water, 
and it's all done.

208
00:17:01,280 --> 00:17:02,110
FINISHED!

209
00:17:02,700 --> 00:17:04,200
How is it?

210
00:17:05,530 --> 00:17:06,990
It's so-so!

211
00:17:07,069 --> 00:17:08,859
You're a harsh critic.

212
00:17:08,950 --> 00:17:11,450
But I don't want it to go to waste, 
so I'll finish it anyway.

213
00:17:11,540 --> 00:17:14,130
How environmentally conscientious.

214
00:17:21,210 --> 00:17:24,010
Okay, I'm starting to feel funny.

215
00:17:24,760 --> 00:17:28,810
To me, the taste of alcohol
is like a bonus.

216
00:17:28,890 --> 00:17:32,390
Just the runway leading to bliss.

217
00:17:32,480 --> 00:17:35,110
I think I'm going to lie down
for a little bit.

218
00:17:36,230 --> 00:17:41,400
Maybe it's about time I let happiness
embrace me, too.

219
00:17:42,490 --> 00:17:43,530
DEMON LIGHT

220
00:18:35,830 --> 00:18:38,710
Aruko! I need some booze!

221
00:18:39,790 --> 00:18:41,960
I went out for drinks, but it sucked.

222
00:18:42,040 --> 00:18:43,460
There was an opening for a joke, 

223
00:18:43,550 --> 00:18:45,930
so when I made one, 
they called me desperate for laughs.

224
00:18:46,010 --> 00:18:48,560
It was totally not the timing
for a roast there!

225
00:18:48,630 --> 00:18:52,510
I can't believe how lame they were
going for the easy laugh.

226
00:18:52,600 --> 00:18:54,310
It was so boring, 

227
00:18:54,930 --> 00:18:57,600
I thought I was close to death.

228
00:19:04,320 --> 00:19:07,160
But not as close to death as you!

229
00:19:07,240 --> 00:19:08,120
RECOVERY POSITION

230
00:19:08,200 --> 00:19:10,040
You're so desperate for laughs.

231
00:19:14,290 --> 00:19:17,080
Chainsmoker Cat!

232
00:19:19,790 --> 00:19:23,130
Greetings, residents of Nyagamihara.

233
00:19:24,040 --> 00:19:25,710
This is a public broadcast.

234
00:19:26,550 --> 00:19:29,760
The air is very dry today.

235
00:19:30,590 --> 00:19:33,130
Please be mindful of fires.

236
00:19:34,180 --> 00:19:37,470
You should especially make sure to put out
your cigarette before discarding.

237
00:19:38,730 --> 00:19:42,690
You have such a beautiful voice.

238
00:19:42,770 --> 00:19:45,190
It sounds put on.

239
00:19:45,270 --> 00:19:47,860
Hey, thanks again for helping.

240
00:19:47,940 --> 00:19:50,480
Apparently, the person
who usually does this

241
00:19:50,570 --> 00:19:53,360
threw their back out "exercising."

242
00:19:53,450 --> 00:19:54,490
Exercising?

243
00:19:54,580 --> 00:19:55,830
Probably ran too much.

244
00:19:55,910 --> 00:19:57,490
What an idiot.

245
00:20:00,660 --> 00:20:03,660
Yaniko! Don't fart in enclosed spaces!

246
00:20:04,340 --> 00:20:06,340
Yakuko, open all the windows!

247
00:20:06,420 --> 00:20:07,960
Okay!

248
00:20:11,930 --> 00:20:15,680
If we broadcast the fart sound
through the mic, that'd be hilarious.

249
00:20:16,260 --> 00:20:17,850
Yaniko, point your butt at me!

250
00:20:18,890 --> 00:20:20,890
Lift it up more!

251
00:20:21,390 --> 00:20:24,480
Now, blast out another big one!

252
00:20:24,560 --> 00:20:27,100
Let your fart echo
throughout the neighborhood!

253
00:20:27,190 --> 00:20:28,480
It's gonna be hilarious.

254
00:20:29,240 --> 00:20:31,580
I don't have any left in me.

255
00:20:31,650 --> 00:20:33,360
I'll buy you smokes if you rip a good one.

256
00:20:42,620 --> 00:20:44,660
You actually farted! That was so loud!

257
00:20:44,750 --> 00:20:46,840
I think that reached the whole city!

258
00:20:46,920 --> 00:20:50,550
Keep ripping more! I'll buy you a pack
for each one you rip!

259
00:20:56,260 --> 00:21:00,560
Okay, that's enough!
My stomach hurts from laughing!

260
00:21:02,350 --> 00:21:05,310
Wait, that was more than a fart!

261
00:21:07,690 --> 00:21:09,110
I can't do this anymore!

262
00:21:12,400 --> 00:21:14,570
Stop, you're letting out too much!

263
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:24,500
What now?

264
00:21:24,580 --> 00:21:26,000
I'm stuck.

265
00:21:26,080 --> 00:21:27,830
Could you push me through?

